 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.3333333333333333,
   "dur": 4.155,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Every breakout starts in one place: a single pore. Let's go inside."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.633333333333334,
   "dur": 9.496,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "This is a healthy pore. A hair, an oil gland at its base, and oil flowing up and out onto your skin. As long as the oil keeps moving, the pore stays clear."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 16.633333333333333,
   "dur": 11.551,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Now add dead skin cells. They mix with the oil and pack the pore shut. Open to the air, the plug oxidizes dark: a blackhead. Closed over by skin, it stays pale: a whitehead."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 31.3,
   "dur": 5.934,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Trapped oil is food. Bacteria feed on it, and the wall swells red: a papule. Then, a pustule."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 41.63333333333333,
   "dur": 6.093,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "So how does it clear? Mandelic acid keeps the pore clear. Benzoyl peroxide clears the bacteria."
